; catalog-api.t27 owns the transport surface. RIDEABLE_SOURCE above is not a copy of a table but
; a COMPOSITION of two things that contract declares -- its LIST_ENDPOINT path and the fourth of
; its FILTER_NAMES -- welded into one query string. That is still a restatement a grep for
; "available_only" finds in two files, so the owner is named here and the two owned literals are
; pinned below. Composition, not copy: COPY_COUNT does not move, and the test asserts that
; RIDEABLE_SOURCE is NOT equal to the endpoint it is built from.
; THE OWNER'S ARRAY MOVED UNDER THIS EDGE, AND THE PIN HELD (re-measured 2026-09-21). On
; 2026-09-20 catalog-api declared FILTER_NAMES as five elements: class, cc_min, cc_max,
; available_only, for_sale. It declares four today: class, min_cc, max_cc, available_only. Two of
; the words were corrected against the shipped endpoint, which had never read the old spellings,
; and for_sale left the filter vocabulary entirely because no query parse mentions it. The fourth
; element survived both changes, so the composition above is still the composition it claims to
; be and nothing here had to move.
; That is the good outcome, and it is recorded as a measurement rather than as reassurance. An
; array this edge depends on lost a fifth of its length and had two of its words rewritten inside
; one day, and the only reason the edge did not break is that every change fell on the other
; positions. What is pinned below is the VALUE available_only and never the ordinal 3; the ordinal
; is the fragile half, and a reader who reaches for it should know it has already been outlived
; once by the thing it indexes.
