; half of the rule. RIDEABLE_RULE and MIN_UNITS_AVAILABLE_TO_RIDE above are half of that rule
; written a second time -- the conjunction in prose and the floor as a number. The audit above did
; not name them, and the reason it could not is worth keeping: the owner holds the floor as a bare
; 1 inside has_an_available_unit, not as a constant a length-and-ends pin could reach. Recorded as
; an EDGE and not an eighth copy, for the same reason the composed route is an edge -- no table
; crosses, one number does, and COPY_COUNT does not move. The bookability DECISION is still
; consumed as a parameter (selected_row_respects_live_gate), so nothing here re-derives it; what
; is pinned is only that the floor this file names is the floor the owner enforces.
